<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92846" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῡσῐ-άζω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῡτιάζω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			42(1).77.11
		</span></i>,al. (Epid., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>treat as a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥύσιον</span>, <i>seize, distrain
			upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ ῥυσιάζω, τἀμὰ δ᾽ εὑρίσκω φίλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					523
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				629.20
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), al., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.638
			</span></i>; of <i>plundering</i> a city <i>as reprisal</i> for
			stolen property, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					8.7
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be so treated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				424
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1406
			</span></i>, <u>IG</u>l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί
				ῥυσιασθείς</span>; <i>robbed of</i> what? cj. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				163
			</span></i>; of debtors at Rome, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cor.</u>
				5
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψευδόδειπνα . . μαργώσης
				γνάθου ἐρρυσιάσθη</span> cj. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				258
			</span></i>.</div>
